.SH NAME
fm-alter - Remove fields


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfm alter \&... drop [, ]... [where ] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes one or more fields from each matching file's frontmatter and writes the
result back to disk. When a field carries a type annotation (field:type), it is only
removed if the stored value matches that type.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for alter


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	Verbosity: -v prints modified count, -vv prints each processed file and total


